From 66975d6f0ecbf8bd1a6ce57ce455104ef1e54774 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jolyon Brown <jolyon@limilo.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 01:50:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix function pointer members of global structs

Since the function pointer optimizations (349b10a) the code generator and
the -Ofp analysis take a function pointer's type from its declaration, so
that the type rewritten by FunctionSets::CompleteAnalyze is seen. A member
access to a global struct variable is constant folded to a DT_VARIABLE_REF
of the variable plus an offset, and the variable itself was then used as
the type: assigning w.fn = f failed with "Cannot assign incompatible types
'w' != ...", calling w.fn() with "Not a simple type", and -Ofp crashed.
Members of local structs and p->fn were not affected. The same unwrapping
in GlobalAnalyzer registered no call edge for a call through such a member
(also through a constant index into a global array of function pointers,
or a variable index into an array member), so in native code the callee
could overwrite parameters the caller still needed.

Add Declaration::RefDeclaration, which finds the variable or struct member
a DT_VARIABLE_REF designates by walking the aggregate type to its offset
(arrays, nested structs, bit fields, base classes), and use it where the
type or the slot of a function pointer is taken from a DT_VARIABLE_REF: the
code generator, FunctionSets::Analyze and GlobalAnalyzer::Analyze. The
constant folding itself is unchanged. GlobalAnalyzer falls back to the
expression's type when the member cannot be resolved (a union), so the call
is registered in any case. Keep the const and volatile qualifiers of the
expression's type when the type is taken from the declaration, so assigning
to a function pointer member of a const struct is rejected again.

funcptrmembertest.c covers assignment and calls through s.m(), (*s.m)() and
p->m for global, static and initialized globals, a struct declared with its
variable, nested structs, array members, arrays of structs, bit field
neighbours, a static local, an initialized struct reassigned in one
function and called from another, the call edge of calls through a member,
a constant array index and a variable index into an array member, and -Ofp.
funcptrmemberaddrtest.c covers &w.fn, &w.arr[1], w.arr and w.arr + 1 as
static initializers, two dimensional arrays and an anonymous union member.
funcptrmemberconsttest.c with the funcptrmemberconstconstraints rule checks
that assignments to const members are rejected. funcptrmemberbasetest.cpp
covers a member inherited from a base class.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01J5rsu7nnbQYnRY7GP34gdn
